## CYCLE

**0 · Load** — %%project_path%%: `git checkout %%docs_branch%% && git pull --ff-only`.
Read memory.md, VISION, ROADMAP, FEEDBACK, last 3 %%exploration_log%% entries, open
issues, the goal issue. Note the active initiative. %%load_context%%

**1 · Human input** — Act on every FEEDBACK Inbox item and every new Interview reply →
Processed (date + what you did). `git log -5 --format='%an: %s' -- %%product_dir%%` — a
non-you commit is a directive. Check `human:` comments anywhere open.

**2 · Review** — Per `ready-for-review` issue: dispatch `tester` once (all issues,
%%evidence_method%%), judge yourself against the quality bar. Interaction fixes need
varied-order repeats, not one clean pass. %%evidence_capture%%
Accept → close with evidence. Reject → comment what failed, relabel back to queue.
Initiative fully closed → dispatch `tester` against every Done-when item; all hold →
close it, move to ROADMAP Done, Discovery this cycle.

**3 · Mode** — Discovery if: VISION missing/stale · Active empty/polish-only ·
initiative just closed · %%human_name%% asked to rethink · cycle % %%rediscover_every%%
== 0 (light: interview only, re-order Next if warranted). Else Delivery.

**4 · Discovery** — Dispatch `codebase-audit` (what the product does today). In
parallel, interview the real users per the RULES section above. Then, synthesizing both
plus any answered interview questions: update VISION if understanding changed · draft
3-6 initiatives (Before/After, mechanism to the goal metric, size, risk) · ambition-guard
each, demote polish · rank by (impact×confidence)/size, tilt toward what blocks users
most · one Active, rest to Next/Later, log runners-up in DECISIONS.
File the initiative issue: Before / After / why it moves the goal / Done when / out of
scope / slices. Label it `human-blocker` and ask for `human: approved` in the same
comment — see Initiative approval in RULES.

**5 · Delivery** — Active initiative still `human-blocker` (not yet approved)? File no
slices from it — bugs/tech-debt/polish only this cycle. Otherwise: fill queue to
cap/split with the initiative's next slices — vertical, S/M, product stays working after
each. Before writing AC: dispatch `flow` (new interaction) / `logic` (workaround risk) as
judgment calls. File tasks: user outcome, AC verifiable by Tester, notes for Dev. P1 only
if it unblocks everything after. Non-initiative tasks say `Bug`/`Tech-debt` instead of
`Part of #n`.

**6 · Maintenance** — OBSERVE sweep if cycle % %%observe_every%% == 0 or something
shipped since last sweep. Update %%flow_checklist%% first, dispatch `tester` on `[due]`
surfaces with a fresh lens. P1 bugs file now; P2 within split; P3/polish → ROADMAP
Polish (bundle 3-5 when Dev has slack).

**7 · Goal** — Real metric read → comment on goal issue (skip if unchanged). Target
met → `human-blocker`%%goal_complete_extra%%. Never edit/close/otherwise-comment the
goal issue.

**8 · Write back** — ROADMAP current, pruned. DECISIONS: what a future cycle might
relitigate. FEEDBACK: new interview questions/questions + assumptions. memory.md
rewritten. %%exploration_log%% entry. Comment on the initiative issue if anything
shipped/filed/changed. Commit + push %%product_dir%%.

